{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794828622,"nonce":"lneCLMfVMb9/MKIFHC4eRclEOX4=","title":"A browser agent that fails leaves the page hanging with no output and no exit status","message":"A program that starts a browser agent (`ash_host_agent`, for example hxn's WebGPU shim) blocks in a synchronous wait on the agent's replies. When the agent cannot answer, the page never reaches done or trapped, a runner waits out its timeout, and nothing says why.\n\nReproducer, from hxn's auto-ash check page in headless Chrome with no WebGPU adapter: `requestAdapter` returns null, the program still sends `requestDevice` on the unset handle, the shim's service throws a TypeError, its loop only calls console.error, and no reply is written. The program waits forever.\n\nAsh cannot see inside a shim's own Worker, so the page needs two things from the shim: a start that throws or rejects fails the page, and a `fail(reason)` hook passed to `start()` for what the shim learns later.\n\nBehaviour: the page writes `agent \u003cname\u003e: \u003creason\u003e` to its log (shown even without `?debug`) and its console, terminates the program and the thread agents, and sets the title to `\u003cmodule\u003e — trapped`, which the existing runners already read. A failure after the program finished is ignored. The program worker's own `onerror` ends the page the same way.\n\nhxn's side (drivers 0.2.0): the generated service loop reports a throwing op through `fail`, and requestAdapter rejects on a null adapter.","files":null}]}